    summary: "The remote-mode mockup mounts quit with no frame prop, so it renders bordered (Button.tsx:50 defaults frame=border) while the actionable-mode quit at line 772 is frame=bare. The Layout zone-H rule states the exit is a bare Button 'in every mode and every state'; Frame B accepts '- a mode-dependent button set'; lines 299 and 598 both say 'the same button in the same corner'. The receipt's data-ink-first justification ('the one border left in the dialog's actions is what ranks them') only holds if the solo quit is bare, since a lone bordered button ranks nothing."
  - dimension: correctness
    location: "docs/work/2026-09-04-redesign-run-9-setup-quit.html:397"
    severity: important
    summary: "The Elements prose claims 'the two commands are the screen's only verbatim payloads, declared data-wire=\"shell command\" at the mockup', but only the setup zone m-steps (line 622) carries the marker. The dialog zone m-dialog mounts OFF_CMD through CopyText (line 748) with no data-wire. The rulebook's wire-marker callout requires data-wire on EVERY payload element, so this is both a false statement and a rule violation. The Tier-1 gate cannot see it: xtask/src/doc.rs check_wire_data fails only when data-wire is absent document-wide, so one marker satisfies it trivially."
